cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Global Ransomware Resilience under Constraint: A Monte Carlo Analysis
  of Cybersecurity Defense Portfolios for Healthcare Networks
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it and record the
  exact commit hash used to generate your results.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "NSRI Summer Research Hackathon 2026 Team"
year: 2026
license: MIT
keywords:
  - ransomware resilience
  - healthcare cybersecurity
  - Monte Carlo simulation
  - defensive security
  - budget-constrained optimization
abstract: >-
  A fully synthetic, defensive Monte Carlo simulation study of how
  cybersecurity defense portfolios affect ransomware-style compromise
  propagation and critical-service disruption in modeled healthcare
  networks of different sizes and cyber-capacity levels, including a
  budget-constrained defense optimizer with cost-sensitivity analysis.
  Contains no malware, exploit code, or real-system interaction.
